						const body = "\nMobile access enables employees to access HR functions and complete self-service tasks using smartphones and tablets.\n\n## Mobile Architecture\n\nMobile capabilities include native apps, responsive web interface, and offline capabilities for areas with limited connectivity.\n\n## Mobile Applications\n\nOracle Fusion HCM mobile apps provide employee self-service, manager functions, and HR operations on-the-go.\n\n## Self-Service Capabilities\n\nEmployee self-service on mobile includes personal information updates, leave requests, expense reporting, and profile management.\n\n## Manager Functions\n\nManagers access team information, approve requests, review performance, and manage direct reports from mobile.\n\n## Responsive Design\n\nEnsure responsive interface adapting to various screen sizes and orientations for optimal mobile experience.\n\n## Offline Functionality\n\nEnable limited offline access for critical functions when internet connectivity is unavailable.\n\n## Mobile Security\n\nImplement security for mobile access including authentication, encryption, and remote device management.\n\n## Push Notifications\n\nSend timely notifications for approvals needed, request updates, and important information.\n\n## Performance Optimization\n\nOptimize mobile performance through efficient APIs, data caching, and bandwidth optimization.\n\n## User Experience\n\nDesign intuitive mobile interfaces matching employee expectations for mobile apps.\n\n## Best Practices\n\n1. Design for touch interaction\n2. Minimize data transfer\n3. Test on real devices\n4. Implement proper security\n5. Monitor mobile usage\n\n## Conclusion\n\nEffective mobile implementation enhances employee engagement and improves HR process efficiency.\n";
